From 22d0bd99ce65b98f8592249f0fe513349f6fc444 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:11:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Plane stress: initialize the axial deformation gradient to
 one

In plane stress, a finite strain behaviour written with the deformation
gradient computes the axial component of the deformation gradient and
stores it in the AxialDeformationGradient internal state variable, which
the generic interface of TFEL uses as the axial component of the
deformation gradient at the beginning and at the end of the time step.
As the other internal state variables, it was initialized to zero: the
deformation gradient at the beginning of the first time step was
singular (the conversion of the first or second Piola-Kirchhoff stress
to the Cauchy stress gave NaN), and a behaviour starting a Newton method
from this value failed.

The new getAxialDeformationGradientOffset function returns the offset of
this variable. The states allocated by MGIS (BehaviourData, and
MaterialStateManager when the caller does not provide the internal state
variables) now set it to one. The arrays given by the caller are not
modified: the documentation says that the caller must set it to one.

The SaintVenantKirchhoffElasticity test behaviour supports plane stress:
it computes the axial component by Newton iterations starting from its
value at the beginning of the time step, and stores the Green-Lagrange
strain before it, so that its offset is not zero. DisplacementGradientTest
compares its stresses, axial deformation gradient and tangent operator
with the analytical solution, with F and with H, and checks the initial
values (behaviour data, material data managers with and without an
initializer, both layouts, arrays given by the caller left unchanged).
These checks fail without this change.
