+In plane stress (`PlaneStress` and `AxisymmetricalGeneralisedPlaneStress`
+hypotheses), the axial component of the deformation gradient is computed
+by the behaviour, and the one given in the gradients is ignored (`TFEL`
+5.2 or later). A behaviour written with the deformation gradient stores
+this axial component in the `AxialDeformationGradient` internal state
+variable, which must start from one. The states allocated by `MGIS` set
+it to one, and the `getAxialDeformationGradientOffset` function returns
+its offset.
+A caller that provides its own arrays of internal state variables (see
+the `MaterialDataManagerInitializer` class) must set it to one, as it
+must set the deformation gradient to the identity.
+
